{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":72663,"duration_api_ms":72663,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"cursor\",\n  \"summary\": \"QA and product engineering view of the status-page feature. The repo has no route handlers yet (no app/**/route.ts) and no health/status endpoint. Tests are Vitest with jsdom, and vitest.config.ts only picks up tests/**/*.test.ts(x). proxy.ts runs on almost every path, and lib/supabase/proxy.ts calls supabase.auth.getUser() whenever Supabase is configured, so a new /status page or /api/status endpoint would pay that cost but not be redirected (it is not under /admin, /proveedor or /mis-cotizaciones). Data access must go through lib/data.ts, which falls back to mock when NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL is missing or still the placeholder; the 'API availability' check should follow the same pattern so tests never need a real Supabase. This area owns: acceptance criteria, contract tests for the endpoint's response, component and regression tests for the page, documentation (README, docs/, MASTER_INDEX), a final verify run plus a browser check, and review. The endpoint, the page and the env-var wiring belong to other areas and are listed here only as dependencies.\",\n  \"areas_affected\": [\n    \"tests/ (new Vitest suites: status endpoint contract, status page rendering, environment/version resolution)\",\n    \"vitest.config.ts (read-only check: the include pattern already covers tests/**/*.test.ts(x); no change expected)\",\n    \"proxy.ts and lib/supabase/proxy.ts (regression check only: the status route must stay public and not redirect)\",\n    \"README.md (how to open the status page and call the endpoint)\",\n    \"docs/ (new or extended doc describing the status contract and environment variables)\",\n    \"docs/index/MASTER_INDEX.md (any new docs/*.md must be linked here, or npm run docs:check fails)\",\n    \".env.example (only if new env vars are introduced; a documentation check, owned by infra/backend)\",\n    \"Code review of app/api/status/route.ts (or wherever the endpoint lives), the status page under app/, and any helper in lib/\"\n  ],\n  \"proposed_tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"qa-1-acceptance-criteria\",\n      \"description\": \"Write down and freeze the acceptance criteria before implementation starts: (a) the endpoint returns JSON with availability status, version, environment and a timestamp; (b) it always returns HTTP 200 for the 'ok' and 'degraded' states, with a defined behaviour when the dependency is down (200 with status=down, or 503, to be decided); (c) the response sets Cache-Control: no-store and is rendered dynamically; (d) no secrets or connection strings appear in the response; (e) the page shows all three values, gives a clear 'unavailable' state when the endpoint fails, and is reachable without logging in; (f) it works in mock mode, i.e. with no Supabase credentials.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"qa\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dep-backend-status-contract\",\n      \"description\": \"DEPENDENCY (backend): define the endpoint path and the exact response schema as a TypeScript type in types/index.ts, plus the availability semantics (static info only, or a live Supabase probe with a bounded timeout). QA needs this before writing contract tests.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"backend\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"qa-1-acceptance-criteria\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dep-infra-version-env-source\",\n      \"description\": \"DEPENDENCY (infra): decide where version and environment come from (package.json version, VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA, VERCEL_ENV or NODE_ENV) and what the fallback values are locally. QA needs the closed set of possible environment values to assert against.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infra\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"qa-2-endpoint-contract-tests\",\n      \"description\": \"Add tests/status-api.test.ts that imports the route handler's GET directly and asserts: the response shape matches the shared type; the status values are within the agreed set; version and environment are resolved from stubbed env vars (vi.stubEnv) in development, preview and production; Cache-Control is no-store; the 'down' or 'degraded' path when the availability probe throws or times out (Supabase client mocked); and no field echoes env values beyond the allow-list. Follow the vi.stubEnv placeholder pattern from tests/data-fallback.test.ts for mock mode. If the handler's runtime needs a Node rather than jsdom environment, mark the file with // @vitest-environment node.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"qa\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"dep-backend-status-contract\",\n        \"dep-infra-version-env-source\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"qa-3-page-component-tests\",\n      \"description\": \"Add tests/status-page.test.tsx with @testing-library/react covering the rendered states (operational, degraded or down, endpoint error or loading) and checking that version and environment labels appear. Exact assertions depend on whether frontend builds the page as a Server Component that reads a lib helper or as a client component that fetches the endpoint; a server-rendered page is better tested by unit-testing the helper plus the presentational component.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"qa\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"dep-frontend-status-page\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dep-frontend-status-page\",\n      \"description\": \"DEPENDENCY (frontend): build the user-facing page (for example app/status/page.tsx) with a presentational component that takes the status payload as props, so it can be tested without network or Supabase. Optionally add a footer link (components/layout/Footer.tsx).\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"frontend\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"dep-backend-status-contract\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"qa-4-proxy-regression\",\n      \"description\": \"Regression check: confirm that rutaProtegida() in lib/supabase/proxy.ts does not match the new page or endpoint paths and that they never redirect to /login. Optionally add a unit test for the path-matching logic (it is not exported today; exporting it would be a backend change, so flag it rather than doing it unilaterally).\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"qa\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"dep-backend-status-contract\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"qa-5-documentation\",\n      \"description\": \"Document the feature: a README section with the page URL and endpoint (example curl and response); a short doc under docs/ (or a section in an existing guide) describing the response contract, the status semantics, where version and environment come from, and the caching and security constraints; link any new docs/*.md in docs/index/MASTER_INDEX.md. Check that .env.example covers any new variable.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"qa\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"dep-backend-status-contract\",\n        \"dep-infra-version-env-source\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"qa-6-full-verification-and-browser-pass\",\n      \"description\": \"Run npm run verify (docs, tooling, test, lint, typecheck, build) once, serially, holding the .next/ resource, after all slices land. Then run a browser pass of /status against npm run dev on port 3000 in two configurations: mock mode (placeholder Supabase URL) and with Supabase configured. Record in the report anything left unverified, such as the Vercel preview or production environment labels.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"qa\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"qa-2-endpoint-contract-tests\",\n        \"qa-3-page-component-tests\",\n        \"qa-4-proxy-regression\",\n        \"qa-5-documentation\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"qa-7-code-review\",\n      \"description\": \"Review the endpoint, page and helpers against the acceptance criteria: no direct Supabase queries from components (the architecture rule in PROJECT_GUIDE.md); the availability probe goes through lib/ with a timeout; no secret env vars are read; dynamic rendering and no-store caching are in place; Next 16 route-handler conventions are followed (check node_modules/next/dist/docs/ as AGENTS.md requires); no new npm dependencies; files are added under the repo root, not the nested resuelvelo/ copy.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"qa\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"dep-backend-status-contract\",\n        \"dep-frontend-status-page\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"contracts\": [\n    \"Status response type (shared, ideally in types/index.ts): { status: 'ok' | 'degraded' | 'down'; version: string; environment: 'development' | 'preview' | 'production' | string; timestamp: ISO-8601 string; checks?: { supabase: 'ok' | 'down' | 'mock' } }. Exact field names are to be confirmed by backend; QA tests will be written against the agreed type.\",\n    \"HTTP contract: GET only, no authentication, Content-Type application/json, Cache-Control: no-store. The status code for the 'down' state must be agreed explicitly (200 with a body flag, or 503); tests will assert whichever is chosen.\",\n    \"Mock-mode contract: when NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL is missing or the placeholder, the endpoint must still respond (for example status 'ok' with checks.supabase='mock') without network calls, keeping npm run test hermetic.\",\n    \"Security contract: the response contains only an allow-listed set of non-sensitive values. Never the anon key, DIRECT_CONN_STRING, service keys or raw error messages from Supabase.\",\n    \"Routing contract: the status page and endpoint stay outside rutaProtegida() in lib/supabase/proxy.ts and never redirect.\",\n    \"Documentation contract: every new docs/*.md is linked from docs/index/MASTER_INDEX.md so npm run docs:check passes.\"\n  ],\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"proxy.ts matches the status endpoint and calls supabase.auth.getUser() on every request when Supabase is configured. That adds latency and a hidden Supabase dependency to a health check, and the status page could appear slow or broken because of the proxy rather than the API. Consider excluding the status path from the matcher (backend decision).\",\n    \"A live Supabase probe without a timeout can hang the endpoint and the page; tests must cover the timeout path with a mocked client.\",\n    \"Information disclosure: publicly exposing the exact version or full commit SHA and the environment helps fingerprint the deployment. The level of detail needs a product or security decision.\",\n    \"A nested resuelvelo/ directory duplicates app/, lib/, tests/ and the configs. tsconfig.json includes **/*.ts, so files placed there by mistake would be typechecked but not tested (vitest only includes root tests/). Reviewers must check that new files are at the repo root.\",\n    \"Vitest runs in jsdom; route handlers that use Request, Response or NextResponse may need a per-file node environment. If that is missed, tests can fail for environment reasons rather than real defects.\",\n    \"The repo has no CI workflow (.github/ is absent), so the new tests are only enforced by running npm run verify by hand; regressions can slip in between manual runs.\",\n    \"Environment labels that depend on Vercel system env vars (VERCEL_ENV) cannot be checked locally; preview and production values remain unverified until a deployment, which needs separate authorization.\",\n    \"Caching regressions: if the page or route is accidentally statically rendered at build time, it will show stale version and availability. The build output and a no-store header test should catch this.\"\n  ],\n  \"tests\": [\n    \"tests/status-api.test.ts: GET returns 200 and JSON matching the shared status type in mock mode (placeholder Supabase URL via vi.stubEnv).\",\n    \"tests/status-api.test.ts: environment resolves correctly for stubbed development, preview and production inputs, and the documented fallback applies when nothing is set.\",\n    \"tests/status-api.test.ts: version matches the agreed source (package.json version or a stubbed commit SHA, possibly truncated).\",\n    \"tests/status-api.test.ts: Cache-Control header contains no-store.\",\n    \"tests/status-api.test.ts: with a mocked Supabase probe that rejects or times out, status is 'down' or 'degraded' with the agreed HTTP code, and the body does not leak the raw error message.\",\n    \"tests/status-api.test.ts: the response body contains no anon key, connection string or other env values outside the allow-list (snapshot of keys or explicit negative assertions).\",\n    \"tests/status-page.test.tsx: the presentational component renders the operational state with version and environment labels.\",\n    \"tests/status-page.test.tsx: renders degraded or down states and an error/unavailable state when the payload is missing or the fetch fails.\",\n    \"Regression: the existing suites (tipos, mock, data-fallback, carrito) still pass unchanged.\",\n    \"Regression (manual or unit): the status path is not matched by rutaProtegida() and does not redirect when logged out with Supabase configured.\",\n    \"npm run docs:check passes with the new or updated docs linked in MASTER_INDEX.md.\",\n    \"npm run verify passes in full (including build), and the build output shows the status route as dynamic.\",\n    \"Browser pass: /status renders correctly on localhost:3000 in mock mode and with Supabase configured, and calling the endpoint directly (curl or browser) returns the documented JSON.\"\n  ],\n  \"questions_or_unknowns\": [\n    \"What exactly does 'API availability' mean: the Next.js endpoint simply answering, a live Supabase connectivity or auth probe, or both reported separately?\",\n    \"Should the 'down' state return HTTP 503 (better for external monitors) or 200 with a status field (simpler for the page)?\",\n    \"Where should the backend version come from: package.json version (currently 0.1.0), the git commit SHA (full or short), or a build timestamp?\",\n    \"Which environment values are canonical: VERCEL_ENV (development, preview, production), NODE_ENV, or a custom APP_ENV? What should be shown locally?\",\n    \"Should the page and endpoint be public and unauthenticated, or restricted (for example to admin) given this is a B2B app and the version disclosure concern?\",\n    \"Should the status path be excluded from the proxy.ts matcher to avoid the per-request Supabase auth call?\",\n    \"Page URL and language: /status or a Spanish slug such as /estado, matching existing routes like /como-funciona, and Spanish UI copy?\",\n    \"Should the page link from the footer or navbar, or be reachable only by URL?\",\n    \"Documentation location: a new docs/ file (which must be linked in MASTER_INDEX.md) or a section in README.md and PROJECT_GUIDE.md?\",\n    \"Is the nested resuelvelo/ directory an intentional copy, or stale and safe to ignore? It affects typecheck scope and reviewer guidance.\",\n    \"Is adding a CI workflow in scope, or explicitly out of scope for this feature?\"\n  ]\n}","session_id":"04e53d9b-cf36-4af8-86a2-7c07ae80982e","request_id":"40a556a6-fc4b-482f-bcf8-e33f2e6f384f","usage":{"inputTokens":18,"outputTokens":8012,"cacheReadTokens":301670,"cacheWriteTokens":40692}}
